      <p class="eyebrow">Cine Globe · Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated"><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 27, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy describes information handled by the Cine Globe mobile application and the
        services it uses. It is based on the app's current implementation; it does not promise a
        particular data-retention period or describe features that are not implemented.
      </p>

      <h2>Information handled by the app</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account and sign-in:</strong> account identifiers and information you provide,
          such as your name, email address, and phone number; the sign-in provider; and the
          Firebase user ID. Sign-in is supported with email and password, phone verification, and
          Google Sign-In. Firebase Authentication handles authentication credentials.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Profiles and preferences:</strong> profile names and settings, including
          profile-level preferences and parental-control settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Viewing and library activity:</strong> watch history and playback progress,
          saved titles, and related profile data. For playback metrics, the app can send the
          signed-in user ID, content ID, watched seconds, completion percentage, and date to its
          Firebase backend.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Downloads and device storage:</strong> download details and some profile-scoped
          app data are stored on your device. Downloaded video files are stored locally by the app.
          Some library and watch-history data may also sync to Firebase.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Subscriptions and payments:</strong> the backend records subscription and order
          information such as the plan, amount, order/payment identifiers, status, and subscription
          dates. Razorpay provides the checkout flow. Payment details entered into Razorpay are
          handled by that provider; the app's own checkout integration sends payment identifiers
          and verification information to its backend.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notifications:</strong> if you grant notification permission, the app can obtain
          an Expo push token and associate it with your account, platform, device name/model, and
          registration timestamps for notification delivery.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How information is used</h2>
      <p>
        The app uses this information to authenticate users, maintain profiles and preferences,
        provide streaming and library features, sync viewing progress, manage subscriptions,
        deliver notifications when enabled, and respond to support requests.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and viewing activity</h2>
      <p>
        The implementation records playback sessions and aggregate content metrics, including
        watched duration and completion information, through Firebase Functions and Firestore.
        This is viewing-related measurement. The current app source does not show a separate
        general-purpose Firebase Analytics event integration.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Cine Globe uses third-party services to provide app features. Depending on your use of the
        app, these include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Firebase:</strong> authentication, database records, and backend functions.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Sign-In:</strong> sign-in when you choose the Google option.</li>
        <li><strong>Expo Notifications:</strong> push-token registration and notification delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>Razorpay:</strong> subscription checkout and payment processing.</li>
        <li><strong>Mux:</strong> video streaming and related media delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>TMDB:</strong> movie and television catalogue metadata.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers process information as needed to provide their services and under their
        respective terms and privacy notices. If you choose to share a title, your device's share
        interface passes the selected message to the app or person you choose.
      </p>

      <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
      <p>
        Account and app records are stored in the Firebase services used by Cine Globe. Some
        profile-scoped information and downloads are also stored on your device. Payment providers
        may keep their own transaction records.
      </p>
      <p>
        The current app implementation does not define a fixed retention schedule. Data may remain
        in app or provider systems until it is removed or no longer needed, subject to applicable
        legal, accounting, security, and dispute-resolution requirements. Provider retention is
        governed by that provider's policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Cine Globe uses Firebase Authentication and Firebase access controls for account-related
        services and relies on its providers' security measures. No internet transmission or
        storage method can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Keep your sign-in credentials
        private and contact support if you believe your account has been accessed without
        authorization.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
      <p>
        You can control notification permission through your device settings and manage available
        profile, library, watch-history, and download items in the app. You may also contact
        support to request access to, correction of, or deletion of account information. The app
        does not currently provide a self-service account-deletion flow or automatically remove
        all account records when a request is emailed. See the
        <a href="cine-globe-delete-account.html">Cine Globe account-deletion page</a> for how to
        submit a request and the current limitations.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe a child has provided personal information through Cine Globe, contact
        support so the concern can be reviewed.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated when the app or its practices change. Questions and privacy
        requests can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:support@bookmywebsite.in">support@bookmywebsite.in</a>.
      </p>
